[31m+ ## Bug and Regression Loops[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - For a reported bug, first diagnose why existing tests missed it. Name the responsible standardized test or scenario and its missing inputs, lifecycle, fixture or assertion; record the coverage gap before product repair.[39m
[31m+ - Strengthen the existing standardized test and shared fixtures or assertions using the project's Harness scenario, state, viewport, registered-test and evidence format. Do not add a one-off bug-specific regression test.[39m
[31m+ - If no existing test covers the behavior, explain the missing coverage category and extend reusable standardized coverage before product repair.[39m
[31m+ - Run the strengthened test against the broken implementation and record the failing command, assertion and observed result before repair. A fixture or environment error is not defect proof; never manufacture a failure.[39m
[31m+ - Before changing product code, commit the failing test separately. Run harness loop record <loop> --phase red --test <path> --command <command> --assertion <actual failure> on that commit. Then make a separate fix commit and run loop record --phase green: the tests, fixtures, command and environment must be unchanged. Preserve both commits when landing; do not squash away the failing-test commit. Focused regression results do not replace full verification.[39m
[31m+ - Repair the product while keeping the strengthened test unchanged. Repeat repair and the same unchanged test until it passes; retain failing and passing evidence at their tested revisions, then run normal verification.[39m
[31m+ - When correcting function names or APIs, parameter names describe their domain role; rename source declarations and update callers and contracts, rather than inventing display labels. Diagnose why the original name or API was accepted, then repair the earliest responsible generator, skill or review checkpoint within the authorized project scope. Verify the revised guidance is emitted for generated projects.[39m
[31m+ - For helper catalogs, prove one selected callable per detail page: distinct links for functions sharing a source module, only that callable’s parameters, return and throws, and selection retained across tabs and revisions. Keep module ownership/history explicit; a missing callable must not silently show a sibling.[39m
[31m+ - During read-only planning, report the coverage diagnosis and propose the standardized test change; do not edit tests or product source. Write only within an approved implementation request.[39m
[31m+ - Use `harness loop create <name> --from bug-fix --goal <text>` for bug repairs: reproduce with a failing test before implementation, then repeat repair and the same unchanged test until it passes.[39m
[31m+ - Use `--from regression-prevention` for regressions requiring durable prevention: identify the root cause, propose the repair and guard, implement both, and include the guard in normal project verification.[39m
[31m+ - Prove the guard rejects reintroducing the original failure in an isolated fixture or temporary workspace; restore the repair and prove the guard passes.[39m
[31m+ - Record failing and passing commands, assertions, and results as step evidence. Keep green/guard/verification steps pending while proof fails; the agent retries repairs and checks. Harness does not launch an AI repair runner or automatically complete steps.[39m
[31m+ - For affected UI paths, exercise the browser flow and capture fresh screenshots, then inspect the images before recording proof. Report blockers without claiming completion.[39m
[31m+ - Browser normal flows, including screenshot/video runs, must have no unexpected console.error or pageerror events. Use the shared browserTest fixture; watch extra contexts before navigation. Keep logs for expected errors and declare their exact messages and reasons in that test. For unexpected errors, prove a failing log assertion before repair, then rerun the same unchanged regression until the error disappears; preserve diagnostics and keep verification pending while errors remain.[39m
[31m+ - Shared browser fixtures must preserve lazy setup. When their dependencies change, prove API-only tests run with an unavailable browser executable alongside actual browser cases.[39m
