[31m+ ## Required Harness Workflow[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Read this file and the `.codex/skills/harness/SKILL.md` skill before changing code.[39m
[31m+ - Use Harness generators for supported code shapes instead of hand-rolling new structure.[39m
[31m+ - Ask `harness info <topic>` before adding unfamiliar code or choosing a scaffold shape.[39m
[31m+ - For non-trivial work, ask what the loop should prove, search templates, then create or continue a `harness loop`.[39m
[31m+ - Add or update a feature spec before implementation.[39m
[31m+ - Keep files small, focused, and aligned with `harness.audit.json` limits.[39m
[31m+ - Run `bun run check` before handing work back; it includes formatting, type checks, lint, tests, build, and `bun run audit`.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ## Clean Code Review[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Use `harness info clean-code` for optional Jev reviews.[39m
[31m+ - Preview with `harness audit . --clean-code --dry-run`; reviews remain disabled until enabled.[39m
[31m+ - Configure a project-owned credential and assess advisory results before enabling the gate.[39m
[31m+ - Keep uncertain judgments visible and never call incomplete reviews clean.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ## Scaffold export coherence[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Change generated source, tests and public export plans together. Verify every generated export targets an emitted scaffold and run the standard focused CLI project-check scenario after a scaffold shape change.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ## Helper implementation ownership[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Public shared helper implementations belong under src/helpers/<responsibility>/<camelName>.ts, with pure functions separated from component/service orchestration. Keep single-consumer helpers with their owner. Point helper source contracts and Source tabs only at the selected callable implementation, never all files of its owning module. Preserve supported import addresses with forwarding exports when needed; update active callers to the canonical helper source. Run the registry helper-source guard and the standard selected-helper Source browser test.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ## Callable usage examples[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Every public helper needs committed usage examples in its callable contract: a real call, argument values, and expected output or error. Verify examples against the implementation; never invent outcomes.[39m
[31m+ - Use descriptive behavior titles, never numbered placeholders. Choose one representative example per distinct behavior; combine redundant inputs. Review the implementation to identify features, including meaningful error or empty states. Equal outputs alone do not establish duplication. Keep exhaustive boundary cases in tests, not the Examples tab.[39m
[31m+ - Run `harness units check`: missing helper examples, placeholder titles and repeated titles or calls must fail. Re-indexing must preserve authored examples. Each helper detail page shows only its own examples at the viewed commit.[39m
